1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,623
Teacher midterm practice, question 36.

2
00:00:04,243 --> 00:00:07,661
True or false: a metallic solid solution is composed

3
00:00:07,661 --> 00:00:11,141
of two phases: the solute and the precipitate.

4
00:00:12,841 --> 00:00:15,381
A solid solution is a single phase.

5
00:00:15,381 --> 00:00:19,977
The solute atoms sit inside the solvent crystal, either substituting for

6
00:00:19,977 --> 00:00:25,118
solvent atoms or in interstitial sites, and the crystal structure is kept.

7
00:00:25,738 --> 00:00:28,651
A precipitate only forms when the solubility limit

8
00:00:28,651 --> 00:00:31,973
is exceeded, and then you have a second phase.

9
00:00:31,973 --> 00:00:34,595
So it is not part of a solid solution.

10
00:00:36,195 --> 00:00:38,091
So the answer is B: false.

11
00:00:38,911 --> 00:00:41,015
Two elements do not mean two phases.
